*---------------------------------------------------------------
* cptree.equ -- CPT_MAXDEP and the CPT_ERR reason codes, split
* out of cptreebss.s and cptree.s so they are `put` BEFORE the
* code that tests them with `cmp #...`.
*
* Same hazard as inc/readdir.equ: real Merlin-8 rejects a
* forward `equ` reference in an immediate operand, merlin32 does
* not. cp.s and mv.s both `cmp #CPTE_LONG` well above their
* `put` of cptree.s, and cptree.s itself tests `#CPT_MAXDEP`
* which cptreebss.s (the dum arena, necessarily last) defined.
* Byte-neutral: an `equ` emits nothing.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* -- Walk depth cap. ProDOS caps an MLI pathname at 64
* -- characters, so with real 15-character component names the
* -- reachable depth is a handful of levels. Exceeding it is a
* -- LOUD failure, never a truncated walk.
CPT_MAXDEP  equ   8

* -- CPT_ERR REASON CODES. A real MLI errno is always < $80, so
* -- the two maux-side refusals take values no MLI call can
* -- return and the consumer can tell them apart without a
* -- second flag.
CPTE_LONG   equ   $F0        ;a child path exceeds MLI_PTH_MAXLN
CPTE_DEEP   equ   $F1        ;the walk hit CPT_MAXDEP

* -- moved from cptreebss.s 2026-08-29: cptree.s uses both,
* -- and a REL module cannot export an equate (Merlin-8 ENT is
* -- code labels only).
CPT_BUFSZ   equ   512
CPT_RECSZ   equ   32

* -- MLI errno $47, duplicate filename (P8 TRM ch. 4's CREATE
* -- error table). Moved here from cptree.s 2026-09-01: the
* -- cptree2.s split made it a cross-module reference, and REL
* -- cannot export an equate. mv.s/cp.s still declare their own
* -- ERR_DUPFN -- a liba module may not depend on a consumer's
* -- equates, and vice versa.
CPT_EDUP    equ   $47

* -- volume-directory storage_type. No house constant exists for
* -- this one; ls.s and file.s set the precedent of spelling it
* -- inline next to STYP_DIR. Same move, same reason.
CPT_STYPVOL equ   $0F
